From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:14:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 064/148] ci: install gc from its release archive instead of
 building it (gcp-m0ei)

Seven runner pods were evicted in 36 minutes on 2026-09-03, every one of them
at the `Install Gas City` step, with kubelet stating the cause verbatim:
"Container runner exceeded its local ephemeral storage limit \"4Gi\"". The
12:56:30Z eviction lands in the same second as run 33757782065's
`##[error]Process completed with exit code 130` -- 128+SIGINT, the pod being
evicted out from under an in-flight `go install`, which GitHub then rendered as
"The operation was canceled" with no cause. Both crons armed by gcp-5yma were
red on their first day.

This is not the gcp-sq1r memory OOM: `dmesg` over the window that brackets all
seven evictions reports zero OOM kills. It is disk.

Measured the step cold on linux/amd64 (anvil, Go 1.26, isolated GOMODCACHE and
GOCACHE) to establish rather than assume the cost:

    go install github.com/gastownhall/gascity/cmd/gc@main
      GOMODCACHE   2.32 GiB     (gc links Dolt: arrow, thrift, aws-sdk-go-v2,
      GOCACHE      1.89 GiB      cloud.google.com/go, envoyproxy, otel, ...)
      gc binary    252 MiB
      total        4.46 GiB      in 1m38s on 16 cores
    release archive install
      tarball      44 MiB (deleted after extraction)
      gc binary    125 MiB (stripped)
      total       ~170 MiB       in 2.3s

The build does not fit in the 4Gi container limit on its own, before the two
checkouts, the Go toolchain, Node, dolt, bd and claude are counted. That also
retires the bead's open hypothesis about which earlier step tipped it over:
none had to. It equally explains why push/PR CI only mostly survived -- ci.yml
ran the same install and was sitting on the cliff, not clear of it.

The 4Gi limit itself is correct and is left alone. Its own comment records that
before it existed a 5.5G renovate clone crossed kubelet's nodefs line and
evicted nine unrelated pods while sparing the culprit. Raising it is the
Overseer's lane in bastion, and is not needed if the step stops asking for
4.46 GiB.

Instead `gc` joins the tools that already install as verified prebuilt archives
-- dolt, bd and claude, via gastownhall/gascity's install-*-archive.sh. The new
.github/scripts/install-gascity-archive.sh follows those scripts closely
(platform tuple, checksum verification, --cache into RUNNER_TOOL_CACHE +
GITHUB_PATH, a final `gc version`) and maps the workflows' documented
GASCITY_REF values onto published releases: main/edge to the rolling `edge`
pre-release, latest via the /releases/latest redirect, and vX.Y.Z or X.Y.Z to
that tag. It exports the resolved path as GC_BIN, so callers stop reaching
through `go env GOPATH`, which the archive install never populates.

Two details worth naming. The tool-cache key includes the checksum, not just
the tag: `edge` is rolling and a tag-only key would serve a stale gc for the
rest of a runner's life. And the bearer token is confined to the api.github.com
request -- a release download redirects to objects.githubusercontent.com and
curl -L replays custom headers onto the redirect target, so a blanket auth
header would hand the token to another host. Everything fetched here is public;
the token is only a rate-limit courtesy, and the script works without one.

A ref with no published archive (a branch, a commit sha) still falls back to
`go install`, loudly, warning about the disk cost. That path is only reachable
from a manual workflow_dispatch against an unreleased gascity ref; no scheduled
run takes it. Keeping it means this change does not quietly narrow the
documented "ref/version" input, and it is why actions/setup-go stays in all
four workflows -- the nightly needs `go` anyway, for the gate's
`go version -m` gc/bd compatibility check.

Guarded by two tests in tests/test_gascity_pack_inference_gate.py, alongside
the existing runner-label sweep. The first is tree-wide for the same reason
that one is: the regression that matters is the workflow added later, which
would otherwise go red at 3am rather than here. Verified red against the
pre-change workflows ("ci.yml: builds gc from source: go install
github.com/gastownhall/gascity/cmd/gc@latest") and green after.

Validation: the installer exercised end to end, unauthenticated, on darwin/arm64
for latest, v1.4.1 and 1.4.1 (all three resolving to one cached binary) and on
anvil linux/amd64 for main -> edge, including the cache-hit path and the
go-install fallback branch; shellcheck clean; validate_registry.py --require-git
ok; the full ci.yml Python suite at 840 passed / 9483 subtests.

Follow-up, not taken here: pack-release-compatibility.yml's actions/setup-go now
has no in-workflow Go consumer except the fallback, so dropping it would free
the toolchain's share of the same 4Gi -- deferred rather than bundled, since it
is a separate claim needing its own verification. Also filed: a load-sensitive
2s subprocess timeout in gascity/tests/test_formula_assets.py that flakes under
full-suite load and passes in isolation, unrelated to this diff.
